{
  "book": "PRO",
  "chapter": 26,
  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-0d589d3e739b6710": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-467",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The hinges of Eastern houses are not like ours, but consist of pivots inserted into sockets both above and below. In the Hauran there are still standing stone houses with stone slabs for doors, having pivots cut out of the same and turning in sockets prepared for them in the wall…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-467",
          "sourceHash": "bfc201b595c5016ab9bf9b31418e3181f9215b7f89fe30a077d0b8e039e95853",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-39063fd96b39e238": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-468",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The number seven is used frequently in Scripture, and expresses the idea of completeness or fullness. Thus the text represents the hypocrite as having a heart filled with abominations. This figurative use of the number seven obtains in some parts of the East at the present day. I…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-468",
          "sourceHash": "f5043538b22b760c8339866fe9c62f1db6b522d09811c6845f3b0d2967152bdb",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      }
    },
